The class `BlockingFirstObserver` is a lightweight, side‑effect‑free observer implementation whose methods (`onNext`, `onError`) contain only a few field assignments and a call to `countDown()`. These operations are trivial and tightly coupled to the surrounding RxJava infrastructure, making isolated micro‑benchmarking of this class not meaningful. Moreover, performance of such observers is typically dominated by the surrounding reactive pipeline rather than the observer itself, so a dedicated JMH benchmark would not provide useful insight.